    "summary": "Plan-only ACCEPT for intended plan-review-15.json. The corrected specification and complete plan set follow the explicit ordinary-Web decision: generator prepare/select remains independent with Web stopped and exact authorized target/batch binding; Web starts with only its ordinary DefaultConnection configured, retains Identity/domain migrations, role seeding, browser authorization and provider administration, and requires no October mode, batch, setup credentials or generator provider document. The explicit architecture classification is warranted by the host composition, database lifetime and O-FR17 changes. ID-I06, ID-S01 and ID-T02 pin final Build-time connection capture across Identity/domain/factory contexts, reload resistance, supported test substitutions and actual Web A/B process proof. The current Program exposes the planned ConfigureServices and deferred ConfigureContainer seams; source-adapter session ownership and current verification remain consistent with the integrated Story 18.1 issuer and three functions. Verification routes follow accepted behavior: changed Web startup and database selection require public-host RED/GREEN; already correct generator/source/provider behavior uses passing regression; unused glue removal uses proportionate direct or refactor checks. No arbitrary artifact-byte/hash test obligation is introduced. Ordered prior raw P-18.4-01–05 and D-18.4-01–05 findings were compared with current artifacts; their plan meanings remain resolved, while superseded tasks require later reconciliation and complete-definition review. Read-only SpecKit prerequisites selected feature017 and its complete plan set; full tasks analysis was withheld in plan-only mode because current tasks belong to the superseded plan. The deterministic workflow plan-content and plan-review dispatch guard passed. HEAD, all twelve artifact hashes and the nonrecursive explicit-path diff SHA-256 match the pinned manifest. No build, test, database, process or provider execution was performed. Acceptance advances to the applicable fresh planned-change authorization; it does not approve implementation or close recovery."
